{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"5fa1192c-b538-44bf-92fd-a5a618af7f23","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Choose two endpoints on a circle. Joining them to a third point on the circle creates an inscribed angle.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Inscribed angle theorem"},{"op":"diagram","id":"circle","region":"right","primitives":[{"kind":"ellipse","center":[0.5,0.5],"radius":[0.36,0.36],"stroke":"solid"},{"kind":"point","at":[0.18823,0.68],"label":"A"},{"kind":"point","at":[0.81177,0.68],"label":"B"},{"kind":"point","at":[0.5,0.14],"label":"P"},{"kind":"point","at":[0.5,0.5],"label":"O"},{"kind":"line","points":[[0.18823,0.68],[0.5,0.14],[0.81177,0.68]],"stroke":"solid","meaning":"Chords forming the inscribed angle APB"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"5fa1192c-b538-44bf-92fd-a5a618af7f23","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Now connect the center to those same endpoints. The central angle and inscribed angle intercept the same lower arc.","ops":[{"op":"line","id":"radius_a","canvas_id":"circle","from":[0.5,0.5],"to":[0.18823,0.68],"stroke":"solid"},{"op":"line","id":"radius_b","canvas_id":"circle","from":[0.5,0.5],"to":[0.81177,0.68],"stroke":"solid"},{"op":"equation","id":"rule","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\angle APB=\\frac12\\angle AOB"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"If the central angle is 120 degrees, what is the inscribed angle intercepting the same arc?","expected_gist":"60 degrees, half the central angle."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"5fa1192c-b538-44bf-92fd-a5a618af7f23","step":{"id":"s3","script":"The inscribed angle is half the central angle intercepting the same arc. So a central angle of 120 degrees gives 60 degrees.","ops":[{"op":"angle_arc","id":"central","canvas_id":"circle","center":[0.5,0.5],"radius":0.12,"start_deg":30,"end_deg":150,"stroke":"solid","label":"120°"},{"op":"angle_arc","id":"inscribed","canvas_id":"circle","center":[0.5,0.14],"radius":0.13,"start_deg":60,"end_deg":120,"stroke":"solid","label":"60°"},{"op":"equation","id":"example","anchor":{"el":"rule","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\angle APB=\\frac{120^\\circ}{2}=60^\\circ"}],"checkpoint":null}}
